---
/* The held close-up: the worn scene with the camera pushed in, and the badge
   turned and held up, nearly filling the window. A back page's content is read
   through the badge's window and scrolls with the page's own scroll; these
   fixed layers sit over it and hide whatever has scrolled out of the window.

   Only on a qualifying desktop (scene/gate.ts); elsewhere it is display: none,
   so phones, touch screens and short windows keep today's back page. CSS and
   markup only: back pages ship no scripts.

   Layers, back to front (z-index tokens in held-view.css):
     the back content (in the page's flow)
     < surround: the scene, then the hand behind the badge, around the window
     < badge: the board around the window, and the window's edge
     < the pinned strip (part of the back content, badge-back.css)
     < the hand in front of the badge
   The hand is two static images of v10's final grip (scene/hand/held-hand.ts):
   decorative, never focusable, and it takes no pointer events, so the content
   under a finger stays clickable.
   The badge's content follows this element (`.held-view ~ .back-face`).

   Rendered by back pages (BackLayout.astro) and in the front's back slot
   (BadgeFront.astro), where a flipped-in back page's face is placed after
   it: the hand turn and the held turn (flip/hand-turn.ts, held-turn.ts) land
   in this same markup. */
import '../../styles/held-view.css';
import WornScene from './WornScene.astro';
import { HELD_HAND } from '../../scene/hand/held-hand';

/** Where the hand's images sit on the held badge, in its units (held-view.css places them). */
const { box } = HELD_HAND;
const handBox = `--hand-x: ${box.x}; --hand-y: ${box.y}; --hand-w: ${box.width}; --hand-h: ${box.height}`;
---

<div class="held-view">
  <!-- Not purely decorative: it hides the content scrolled out of the window
       and takes the clicks meant for what it hides. Never focusable. -->
  <div class="held-view__surround" aria-hidden="true">
    <WornScene />
    <div class="held-view__hand held-view__hand--behind" style={handBox}></div>
  </div>
  <div class="held-view__badge" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="held-view__window" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="held-view__hand held-view__hand--front" style={handBox} aria-hidden="true"></div>
</div>
